Application Hosting Options in Azure

Azure provides different ways to host applications depending on control, scalability, and complexity.

1. Virtual Machines (VMs)
Full control over OS and environment
You manage updates, scaling, and maintenance

Use when you need maximum control

2. App Service
Platform for hosting web apps, APIs, and mobile backends
No infrastructure management
Built-in scaling and security

Best for web applications and REST APIs

3. Azure Functions
Serverless, event-driven code
Runs only when triggered
Automatically scales

Ideal for small tasks and automation

4. Containers (Azure Kubernetes Service / Container Instances)
Run apps in containers
Consistent environments across dev and production
Options:
AKS (Kubernetes) → full orchestration
Container Instances → simple container execution

Use for microservices and modern apps

5. Azure Spring Apps
Fully managed service for Spring Boot applications

👉 Best for Java developers using Spring
